# Docker environment variables for UNILIS.
#
# Copy to .env in this directory (compose reads it automatically) and set real
# values. .env is gitignored — never commit it.
#
#   cp .env.docker.example .env && nano .env
#
# The database passwords below are REQUIRED. docker-compose.yml refuses to start
# without them rather than falling back to a default, because the previous
# hardcoded values were committed to a repository whose .git directory was
# briefly downloadable. Treat any password that was ever in git as compromised.
#
# Generate strong values, e.g.:
#   openssl rand -base64 24

# --- Databases (required) ---
MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD=
MYSQL_PASSWORD=
SMARTLAB_MYSQL_PASSWORD=

# Changing these AFTER first startup does not update the existing MySQL volume:
# the entrypoint only applies them when initialising an empty data directory.
# To rotate on a live database, ALTER USER inside the container, then update .env
# so both sides match.

# --- Meeting Python media server ---
# Port exposed on the host (must match docker-compose meeting-server ports)
MEETING_MEDIA_PORT=8765

# Full WebSocket URL for browsers. Leave unset to auto-detect from HTTP_HOST.
# Local Docker: ws://localhost:8765/ws/media (auto-detected)
# Production HTTPS example:
# MEETING_MEDIA_WS_URL=wss://your-domain.com:8765/ws/media

# --- App database host (compose service names) ---
# DB_HOST=db
# SMARTLAB_DB_HOST=smart-labs-db
# MYSQL_USER=unilisuser
# MYSQL_DATABASE=unilis
